$DIR/main.p:44:15: cannot pass sharedHolder().p to save, which keeps it after returning
    sharedHolder().p points into the temporary SharedHolder that sharedHolder()
    returns. The SharedHolder made at main.p:44 is a temporary: nothing keeps
    it, so its object is dropped at the end of the statement. A view of the
    object may be passed to calls in that statement but may not outlive it. save
    stores g in package variable saved (main.p:16), so sharedHolder().p would
    outlive the temporary.
    The view does not own the memory it looks at. Nothing keeps the temporary
    after the statement, so a stored view would outlive the value that keeps its
    memory alive.
    Change save to take a value or an owner, which it can keep: an owned[T] from
    new, a shared[T], or a library owner such as a vec.Vec.
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3009" for a longer explanation)
